{"description":"Documents published on or before 11/15/2026","count":10000,"total_pages":50,"next_page_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bpublication_date%5D%5Blte%5D=2026-11-15&format=json&order=newest&page=2&per_page=20&search_after_cursor=WzE3OTQ1MjgwMDAwMDAsIjIwMjYtMjMxODAiXQ","results":[{"title":"Presidential Determination Pursuant to Section 1245(d)(4)(B) and (C) of the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2012","type":"Presidential Document","abstract":null,"document_number":"2026-23233","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23233/presidential-determination-pursuant-to-section-1245d4b-and-c-of-the-national-defense-authorization","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23233.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23233.pdf?1794500111","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"EXECUTIVE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT","name":"Executive Office of the President","id":538,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/executive-office-of-the-president","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/538","parent_id":null,"slug":"executive-office-of-the-president"}],"excerpts":null},{"title":"Airworthiness Directives; The Boeing Company Airplanes","type":"Proposed Rule","abstract":"The FAA proposes to adopt a new airworthiness directive (AD) for certain The Boeing Company Model 787-8 airplanes. This proposed AD was prompted by a report that certain wing skin outer mold line (OML) penetrating fasteners installed using threaded nuts without cap seals do not provide reliable protection against potential ignition sources when subjected to direct attachment lightning currents. This proposed AD would require inspecting between certain ribs on the left and right wing for wing skin penetrating fasteners with a threaded nut adjacent to the electromagnetic effects (EME) sleeve; inspecting the left and right wing fuel tanks, surge tanks, and dry bays for threaded nuts installed on fasteners that penetrate the upper and lower wing skins; accomplishing the inspection specified in a certain airworthiness limitation (AWL); and applicable on-condition actions. This proposed AD would also require accomplishing concurrent requirements and revising the maintenance program to incorporate the airworthiness limitation task. The FAA is proposing this AD to address the unsafe condition on these products.","document_number":"2026-23198","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23198/airworthiness-directives-the-boeing-company-airplanes","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23198.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23198.pdf?1794491123","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","name":"Transportation Department","id":492,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","parent_id":null,"slug":"transportation-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Aviation Administration","name":"Federal Aviation Administration","id":159,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-aviation-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/159","parent_id":492,"slug":"federal-aviation-administration"}],"excerpts":"The FAA proposes to adopt a new airworthiness directive (AD) for certain The Boeing Company Model 787-8 airplanes. This proposed AD was prompted by a report that certain wing skin outer mold line (OML) penetrating fasteners installed using threaded..."},{"title":"Publication of Iran-Related Web General Licenses EE and FF","type":"Rule","abstract":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing two Iran-related general licenses (GLs): GLs EE and FF, which were made available on OFAC's website at the time of issuance.","document_number":"2026-23197","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23197/publication-of-iran-related-web-general-licenses-ee-and-ff","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23197.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23197.pdf?1794491123","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY","name":"Treasury Department","id":497,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/treasury-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/497","parent_id":null,"slug":"treasury-department"},{"raw_name":"Office of Foreign Assets Control","name":"Foreign Assets Control Office","id":203,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/foreign-assets-control-office","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/203","parent_id":497,"slug":"foreign-assets-control-office"}],"excerpts":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing two Iran-related general licenses (GLs): GLs EE and FF, which were made available on OFAC's website at the time of issuance."},{"title":"Publication of Russian Harmful Foreign Activities Sanctions Regulations Web General Licenses 55F and 115D","type":"Rule","abstract":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing two general licenses (GLs) issued pursuant to the Russian Harmful Foreign Activities Sanctions Regulations: GLs 55F and 115D, each of which was previously made available on OFAC's website.","document_number":"2026-23196","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23196/publication-of-russian-harmful-foreign-activities-sanctions-regulations-web-general-licenses-55f-and","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23196.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregiste