ov/agencies/foreign-assets-control-office","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/203","parent_id":497,"slug":"foreign-assets-control-office"}],"excerpts":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing a general license (GL) issued in the Cuba Sanctions program: GL 1. This GL was previously made available on OFAC's website."},{"title":"Amendment of Class C Airspace; Laughlin Air Force Base, Del Rio, TX","type":"Rule","abstract":"This action makes administrative amendments to the Laughlin AFB, TX, Class C airspace legal description. Specifically, the action updates the geographic coordinates of the airport reference point (ARP) to match the FAA's National Airspace System Resources (NASR) database information. Additionally, this action corrects the header format to conform with current FAA policy. Lastly, this action updates the outdated term \"Airport/Facility Directory\" to \"Chart Supplement.\" This action does not change the lateral boundaries, altitudes, or operating requirements of the Class C airspace area.","document_number":"2026-23194","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23194/amendment-of-class-c-airspace-laughlin-air-force-base-del-rio-tx","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23194.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23194.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF TRANSPORTATION","name":"Transportation Department","id":492,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/transportation-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/492","parent_id":null,"slug":"transportation-department"},{"raw_name":"Federal Aviation Administration","name":"Federal Aviation Administration","id":159,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/federal-aviation-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/159","parent_id":492,"slug":"federal-aviation-administration"}],"excerpts":"This action makes administrative amendments to the Laughlin AFB, TX, Class C airspace legal description. Specifically, the action updates the geographic coordinates of the airport reference point (ARP) to match the FAA's National Airspace System..."},{"title":"Publication of Iran-Related Web General License W","type":"Rule","abstract":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing an Iran-related general license (GL): GL W. This GL was previously made available on OFAC's website.","document_number":"2026-23193","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23193/publication-of-iran-related-web-general-license-w","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23193.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23193.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF THE TREASURY","name":"Treasury Department","id":497,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/treasury-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/497","parent_id":null,"slug":"treasury-department"},{"raw_name":"Office of Foreign Assets Control","name":"Foreign Assets Control Office","id":203,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/foreign-assets-control-office","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/203","parent_id":497,"slug":"foreign-assets-control-office"}],"excerpts":"The Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) is publishing an Iran-related general license (GL): GL W. This GL was previously made available on OFAC's website."},{"title":"Agency Information Collection Activities; Submission to the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) for Review and Approval; Comment Request; Electronic Logbook for the Commercial Shrimp Fishery in the Gulf of America","type":"Notice","abstract":"The Department of Commerce, in accordance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), invites the general public and other Federal agencies to comment on proposed, and continuing information collections, which helps us assess the impact of our information collection requirements and minimize the public's reporting burden. The purpose of this notice is to allow for 60 days of public comment preceding submission of the collection to OMB.","document_number":"2026-23192","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23192/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23192.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23192.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE","name":"Commerce Department","id":54,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/commerce-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/54","parent_id":null,"slug":"commerce-department"},{"raw_name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","id":361,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/361","parent_id":54,"slug":"national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration"}],"excerpts":"The Department of Commerce, in accordance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), invites the general public and other Federal agencies to comment on proposed, and continuing information collections, which helps us assess the impact of our..."},{"title":"Agency Information Collection Activities; Submission to the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) for Review and Approval; Comment Request; Mandatory Shrimp Vessel and Gear Characterization Survey","type":"Notice","abstract":"The Department of Commerce, in accordance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), invites the general public and other Federal agencies to comment on proposed, and continuing information collections, which helps us assess the impact of our information collection requirements and minimize the public's reporting burden. The purpose of this notice is to allow for 60 days of public comment preceding submission of the collection to OMB.","document_number":"2026-23191","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23191/agency-information-collection-activities-submission-to-the-office-of-management-and-budget-omb-for","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23191.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23191.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE","name":"Commerce Department","id":54,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/commerce-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/54","parent_id":null,"slug":"commerce-department"},{"raw_name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","name":"National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration","id":361,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/361","parent_id":54,"slug":"national-oceanic-and-atmospheric-administration"}],"excerpts":"The Department of Commerce, in accordance with the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), invites the general public and other Federal agencies to comment on proposed, and continuing information collections, which helps us assess the impact of our..."},{"title":"Final Deauthorization List of Water Resources Projects","type":"Notice","abstract":"The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (Corps) is publishing the final deauthorization list of water resources development projects and separable elements of projects identified for deauthorization in accordance with Section 301 of the Water Resources Development Act (WRDA) of 2020, as amended by Section 1301 of WRDA 2024 (33 U.S.C. 579d-2). The final list was prepared after consideration of the public comments received on the proposed deauthorization list published in the Federal Register on May 21, 2026 (91 FR 29946). The final list has been submitted to the Committee on Transportation and Infrastructure of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Environment and Public Works of the Senate.","document_number":"2026-23190","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23190/final-deauthorization-list-of-water-resources-projects","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23190.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23190.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE","name":"Defense Department","id":103,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/defense-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/103","parent_id":null,"slug":"defense-department"},{"raw_name":"Department of the Army, Corps of Engineers","name":"Engineers Corps","id":142,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/engineers-corps","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/142","parent_id":103,"slug":"engineers-corps"}],"excerpts":"The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (Corps) is publishing the final deauthorization list of water resources development projects and separable elements of projects identified for deauthorization in accordance with Section 301 of the Water Resources..."},{"title":"Agency Information Collection Activities: Proposed Collection; Comment Request","type":"Notice","abstract":"The Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) is announcing an opportunity for the public to comment on CMS' intention to collect information from the public. Under the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), federal agencies are required to publish notice in the Federal Register concerning each proposed collection of information (including each proposed extension or reinstatement of an existing collection of information) and to allow 60 days for public comment on the proposed action. Interested persons are invited to send comments regarding our burden estimates or any other aspect of this collection of information, including the necessity and utility of the proposed information collection for the proper performance of the agency's functions, the accuracy of the estimated burden, ways to enhance the quality, utility, and clarity of the information to be collected, and the use of automated collection techniques or other forms of information technology to minimize the information collection burden.","document_number":"2026-23189","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23189/agency-information-collection-activities-proposed-collection-comment-request","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23189.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23189.pdf?1794491122","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES","name":"Health and Human Services Department","id":221,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/health-and-human-services-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/221","parent_id":null,"slug":"health-and-human-services-department"},{"raw_name":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services","name":"Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services","id":45,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/centers-for-medicare-medicaid-services","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/45","parent_id":221,"slug":"centers-for-medicare-medicaid-services"}],"excerpts":"The Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) is announcing an opportunity for the public to comment on CMS' intention to collect information from the public. Under the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 (PRA), federal agencies are required to..."},{"title":"Self-Regulatory Organizations; MX2 LLC; Notice of Filing and Immediate Effectiveness of a Proposed Rule Change To Amend the Exchange's Fee Schedule","type":"Notice","abstract":null,"document_number":"2026-23188","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23188/self-regulatory-organizations-mx2-llc-notice-of-filing-and-immediate-effectiveness-of-a-proposed","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23188.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23188.pdf?1794491121","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION","name":"Securities and Exchange Commission","id":466,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/securities-and-exchange-commission","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/466","parent_id":null,"slug":"securities-and-exchange-commission"}],"excerpts":null},{"title":"Self-Regulatory Organizations; Investors Exchange LLC; Notice of Filing and Immediate Effectiveness of Proposed Rule Change To Extend the Implementation Timeframe of a Recent Rule Filing","type":"Notice","abstract":null,"document_number":"2026-23187","html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/11/13/2026-23187/self-regulatory-organizations-investors-exchange-llc-notice-of-filing-and-immediate-effectiveness-of","pdf_url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-11-13/pdf/2026-23187.pdf","public_inspection_pdf_url":"https://public-inspection.federalregister.gov/2026-23187.pdf?1794491121","publication_date":"2026-11-13","agencies":[{"raw_name":"SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION","name":"Securities and Exchange Commission","id":466,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/securities-and-exchange-com